WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
Observe, trace, compare, and understand the result in three dimensions.

00:05.000 --> 00:10.000
Read the radiological display first. Patient right appears on screen left.

00:10.000 --> 00:15.000
Review every displayed slice before drawing. Use neighbouring images when a boundary is uncertain.

00:15.000 --> 00:20.000
Contour only the assigned structure. Close each component, then copy to a neighbouring slice and adjust it.

00:20.000 --> 00:25.000
After submission, compare your contour with the reader-1 educational reference using overlap and in-plane boundary metrics.

00:25.000 --> 00:30.000
Then open the matching existing same-study GLB. It is a spatial reference, not a reconstruction of your contour.

00:30.000 --> 00:35.000
Your route is primer, synthetic warm-up, then thirty Prostate158 teaching cases. Targets are supplied and references remain educational.
